    "text": "Outpatient Illness Surveillance: The proportion of outpatient visits for influenza-like illness (ILI) was 1.2%, which is below the national baseline of 2.1%. All 10 regions reported ILI below region-specific baseline levels. Georgia experienced low ILI activity; Puerto Rico, New York City and 47 states experienced minimal ILI activity; and the District of Columbia and two states had insufficient data.\n\nNational ILINet outpatient influenza-like-illness indicators for the 2015-2016 season, weekly from the season start (MMWR week 40) through week 40 (1 weeks to date) — percent of visits for ILI, total ILI visits, and ILI patient counts by age group (0-4, 5-24, 25-49, 50-64, 65+): <ts></ts>.",
